  ($q$cs-97$q$, $q$rw$q$, $q$Craft and Structure$q$, $q$Cross-Text Connections$q$, 2, $q$Text 1: Climatologist A argues that recent Arctic sea ice loss is driven primarily by rising atmospheric temperatures, citing a strong correlation between global temperature records and ice extent over the past forty years.

