  ($q$cs-259$q$, $q$rw$q$, $q$Craft and Structure$q$, $q$Text Structure and Purpose$q$, 2, $q$Early wind turbine blades were short and flat, generating only modest amounts of power. Engineers later discovered that longer, subtly twisted blades captured far more energy from the same wind speed, a design now standard across the industry.$q$, $q$Which choice best describes the overall structure of the text?$q$, $q$["It contrasts an early, limited design with a later improvement that became the industry standard.","It presents two competing theories about wind speed measurement.","It argues that short blades remain superior to long ones.","It compares wind turbines to an unrelated renewable energy source."]$q$::jsonb, 0, $q$The text contrasts the early short, flat blades with the later twisted design that became standard, matching choice A exactly.$q$),
